{"_t": 86800, "operation": 0, "seqid": 73, "answer": "Across the three collections, warmer seasons are raising pest and disease pressure, but the way it shows up differs by industry.\n\nIn fisheries and aquaculture, warmer water is linked to more frequent disease outbreaks in farmed shellfish, with mortality events clustering after long runs of above-average water temperature [block-AA]. Movement controls are now triggered by temperature thresholds rather than calendar dates [block-AB].\n\nIn grains, warm and wet springs bring rust epidemics forward, so the first infections appear before many crops reach the growth stages fungicide programs were timed for [block-AC]. Resistant varieties and early in-crop surveillance are the first line of defence [block-AD].\n\nIn rural industries, the clearest evidence is on heat stress: livestock and honey bee colonies both show losses on runs of hot days, and shade, water and hive placement reduce them [block-AE]. Mild winters also let some pests survive and build up earlier in the season [block-AF].\n\nCommon to all three, the research recommends monitoring tied to temperature triggers rather than fixed dates.", "generated_text": null, "answer_citations": {"metadata": {"block-AA": {"context_id": "ctx-fisheries", "origin_urls": ["https://example.org/fish/res-fish-0412.pdf"], "chunk_index": 0}, "block-AB": {"context_id": "ctx-fisheries", "origin_urls": ["https://example.org/fish/res-fish-0519.pdf"], "chunk_index": 2}, "block-AC": {"context_id": "ctx-grains", "origin_urls": ["https://example.org/grain/res-grain-1108.pdf"], "chunk_index": 0}, "block-AD": {"context_id": "ctx-grains", "origin_urls": ["https://example.org/grain/res-grain-0964.pdf"], "chunk_index": 1}, "block-AE": {"context_id": "ctx-rural-2", "origin_urls": ["https://example.org/rural/res-rural-0310.pdf"], "chunk_index": 0}, "block-AF": {"context_id": "ctx-rural", "origin_urls": ["https://example.org/rural/res-rural-0291.pdf"], "chunk_index": 1}}}}
